LISPTC LANGUAGE REFERENCE

Lisptc: Common-Lisp-like dialect. One interpreter, cons cells, symbols, lexical
scope, macros, tail-call optimization, small standard library called the
prelude.

SYNTAX

Source is s-expressions. (f a b) calls f with evaluated a and b.
Only parenthesised top-level forms are program text. Text around them is prose,
ignored.

DATA

nil = () = null = empty list = the ONLY false value. t canonical true.
Everything except nil truthy, including 0, "", empty structures.

FORMS

Special forms: quote, progn, cond, setq, lambda, macro, quasiquote, try.
Prelude macros, used the same way: if, when, unless, and, or, let, let*,
letrec, while, dolist, dotimes, case, defun, defmacro, setf, push, pop, incf,
decf, block, return-from, catch, unwind-protect. Prelude functions are all available by default.

MEMORIES

Detail for each topic is in built-in memories. Before you use a name or form
from a topic, recall its memory by key: memory/recall "key".
lang/syntax, lang/prose-asides, lang/data-types, lang/special-forms,
lang/numbers, lang/arithmetic, lang/lists, lang/hash-vectors, lang/strings,
lang/json-read, lang/eval-control, lang/output, lang/introspection,
lang/prelude-access, lang/prelude-map, lang/prelude-sort, lang/prelude-build,
lang/prelude-search, lang/prelude-predicates, lang/prelude-alists,
lang/prelude-get-in, lang/prelude-set-in, lang/prelude-branch, lang/prelude-let,
lang/prelude-loops, lang/prelude-defun, lang/prelude-string-search,
lang/prelude-string-edit, lang/prelude-format, lang/places, lang/macros, lang/errors, lang/gotchas.
